 the  officers were concerned that we were  trying to take tools away from them  according to a new york times  investigation in the last five years at  least 400 unarmed drivers and passengers  have been killed by police during  traffic stops nationwide and black  motorists are over represented  it started over a license plate for  dante wright  philando castile was killed at this  traffic stop the officer later said he  thought castile was pulling out a gun oh  my god please don't tell me he's dead in  another escalation a passenger killed  police officer ella french in chicago  you have to ask yourself what are the  consequences we spoke with chesapeake  police chief kelvin wright who called  the state of virginia's ban a slippery  slope things escalated out of control in  just about any type of call we respond  to which tells me that it is a people  problem chief can ask you a somewhat  personal question yes do you have any  kids i have two sons do you have the  talk with them about how they need to  behave themselves uh when interacting  with law enforcement yes ma'am i tell  them these are the things you do to make  sure that you walk away from an  interaction with a police officer okay  there are ways to conduct traffic stops  and all police interactions and minimize  the potential harm but i think it is a  two-way street  right escalation by police and citizens  is the real problem not traffic stops  in lansing low level stops are down but  black drivers are still  disproportionately pulled over but mayor  shore hopes the ban will improve  relations with police a lot of it is a  trust factor our citizens have to be  able to trust the police for cbs  mornings adriana diaz lansing michigan
 

